<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōstĭbŭlum</span></b> ,
			i, n.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A prostitute</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Aul.
				2, 4, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Lev. 21, 7</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a male who
				prostitutes himself</i>, <i><span class="en">Arn. 6,
			199</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A brothel</i>, <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig.
				18, 42, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ezech. 16, 24</span></i>; also, in
			transf. signif., id. Joel, 3, 3.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
